  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "id": "c1-s1",
          "narration": "Welcome to our lesson on recursion! We'll learn how functions can call themselves using a factorial example.",
          "type": "title",
          "heading": "Understanding Recursion",
          "subheading": "Learn how recursion works with a simple factorial example."
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-s2",
          "narration": "Here's our function named factorial. It takes one parameter, n.",
          "type": "code",
          "code": "def factorial(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    return n * factorial(n - 1)\nprint(factorial(3))",
          "highlightLines": [
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-s3",
          "narration": "If n is zero, we return 1. This is called the base case.",
          "type": "code",
          "code": "def factorial(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    return n * factorial(n - 1)\nprint(factorial(3))",
          "highlightLines": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c1-s4",
          "narration": "The base case stops the recursion. Without it, we'd call factorial forever!",
          "type": "code",
          "code": "def factorial(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    return n * factorial(n - 1)\nprint(factorial(3))",
          "highlightLines": [
            3
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "title": "Recursive Call",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "id": "c2-s1",
          "narration": "For other values of n, we return n times the factorial of n minus one. This is the recursive call.",
          "type": "code",
          "code": "def factorial(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    return n * factorial(n - 1)\nprint(factorial(3))",
          "highlightLines": [
            4
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-s2",
          "narration": "Let's run factorial of 3. It calls factorial of 2, which calls factorial of 1, which calls factorial of 0. Each call waits for the one above it.",
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "kind": "callstack",
            "frames": [
              {
                "call": "factorial(3)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "3"
                }
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(2)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "2"
                }
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(1)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "1"
                }
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(0)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "0"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-s3",
          "narration": "First, factorial of 0 returns 1. This is our base case.",
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "kind": "callstack",
            "frames": [
              {
                "call": "factorial(3)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "3"
                }
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(2)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "2"
                }
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(1)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "1"
                }
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(0)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "0"
                },
                "returns": "1"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-s4",
          "narration": "Next, factorial of 1 returns 1. It multiplies n by the result of factorial of 0.",
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "kind": "callstack",
            "frames": [
              {
                "call": "factorial(3)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "3"
                }
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(2)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "2"
                }
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(1)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "1"
                },
                "returns": "1"
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(0)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "0"
                },
                "returns": "1"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-s5",
          "narration": "Then, factorial of 2 returns 2. It multiplies n by the result of factorial of 1.",
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "kind": "callstack",
            "frames": [
              {
                "call": "factorial(3)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "3"
                }
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(2)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "2"
                },
                "returns": "2"
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(1)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "1"
                },
                "returns": "1"
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(0)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "0"
                },
                "returns": "1"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "c2-s6",
          "narration": "Finally, factorial of 3 returns 6. It multiplies n by the result of factorial of 2.",
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "kind": "callstack",
            "frames": [
              {
                "call": "factorial(3)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "3"
                },
                "returns": "6"
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(2)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "2"
                },
                "returns": "2"
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(1)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "1"
                },
                "returns": "1"
              },
              {
                "call": "factorial(0)",
                "vars": {
                  "n": "0"
                },
                "returns": "1"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c3",
      "title": "Output",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "id": "c3-s1",
          "narration": "And here's the result of our program. Factorial of 3 is 6.",
          "type": "output",
          "output": "6"
        },
        {
          "id": "c3-s2",
          "narration": "To wrap up, remember: recursion involves self-calling functions, needs a base case, and builds results from nested calls. Great job learning about recursion!",
          "type": "recap",
          "points": [
            "Recursion is when a function calls itself.",
